Bypass Jekyll on the public mirror's GitHub Pages build.

These pages are hand-authored static HTML with no build step, no Jekyll
front-matter, no Liquid templating and no _layouts. Running them through
Jekyll adds a failure mode and buys nothing.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. GitHub Pages builds for Terranimus/TerranSoul began
failing at 2026-08-06T10:55Z with a bare "Page build failed." Every mirror
push after that succeeded, so the public repo held the current pages while
the live site kept serving the last good build from 10:44 — a 264 KB page
with 39 figures and a 56-entry contents list, against 602 KB, 105 figures
and 114 entries in the repo. The site looked frozen while every check on
the publishing pipeline reported success.

Presence of this file switches Pages to serving the directory verbatim, so
a Jekyll processing error can no longer strand a correct mirror behind a
stale deployment.
